@startuml
title weefs — High-level Bad Design (anti-patterns that were later fixed)

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
hide empty members

' =====================================================================
' UI layer — MVC boundary violated, single-session, no clipboard
' =====================================================================
package "UI (MVC violated)" #FFEBEB {

  class ArchiveModel <<BAD: God object>> <<single-session>> {
    -archive : FileSystem
    -archivePath : Path
    -selectedFile : FileNode
    -readOnly : boolean
    -remoteMounted : boolean
    -nfsConfig : NfsConnectionConfig
    --
    +openArchive(Path) : void
    +closeArchive() : void
    +setNfsConfig(NfsConnectionConfig) : void
    +mountRemote(URI) : void
  }
  note right of ArchiveModel
    One class owns archive state, NFS state,
    UI-selection state, and lifecycle.
    Violates SRP. Only one archive at a time —
    no multi-mount support.
  end note

  class ArchiveController <<BAD: duplicate state>> <<fat controller>> {
    -model : ArchiveModel
    -currentNfsConfig : NfsConnectionConfig
    --
    +extractSelected() : void
    +createDirectory(String) : void
    +deleteSelected() : void
    +renameSelected(String) : void
    +getNfsFileOps() : NfsFileOperations
  }
  note right of ArchiveController
    currentNfsConfig mirrors model.getNfsConfig()
    → two sources of truth.
    Exposes concrete NfsFileOperations → DIP leak.
    No IArchiveController / INfsController split.
  end note

  class NfsFileOperations <<BAD: concrete leak>>
  class FileOperations <<BAD: concrete leak>>
  note bottom of FileOperations
    No IFileOperations abstraction →
    controller & views bind to concrete types.
  end note

  class MainFrame <<BAD: tight coupling>> {
    -controller : ArchiveController
  }
  note bottom of MainFrame
    View holds a concrete controller,
    not an interface.
  end note

  ' --- supporting base classes (unchanged across transition) ---
  class FileNode <<base: tree node>> {
    -name : String
    -path : Path
    -directory : boolean
    -children : List<FileNode>
  }
  class FileType <<base: enum>>
  class FileTypeDetector <<base: util>>
  class ArchiveTreePanel <<base: view>>
  class FileContentPanel <<base: view>>
  class StatusBarPanel <<base: view>>
  class MenuBarFactory <<base: view builder>>
  class ToolBarFactory <<base: view builder>>
  class IconFactory <<base: util>>
  class SwingUtils <<base: util>>
  class WeeFsApp <<base: entry>>
  class NfsConnectionConfig <<base: value object>>
  class NfsConnectionDialog <<base: view>>

  WeeFsApp --> ArchiveModel
  WeeFsApp --> ArchiveController
  WeeFsApp --> MainFrame
  MainFrame --> ArchiveTreePanel
  MainFrame --> FileContentPanel
  MainFrame --> StatusBarPanel
  MainFrame ..> MenuBarFactory
  MainFrame ..> ToolBarFactory
  ArchiveTreePanel --> ArchiveController
  ArchiveTreePanel ..> FileNode
  ArchiveTreePanel ..> IconFactory
  FileContentPanel ..> FileNode
  FileContentPanel ..> FileTypeDetector
  StatusBarPanel --> ArchiveModel
  MenuBarFactory ..> ArchiveController
  ToolBarFactory ..> ArchiveController
  FileTypeDetector --> FileType
  ArchiveModel --> FileNode
  ArchiveModel --> NfsConnectionConfig
  NfsConnectionDialog ..> NfsConnectionConfig
  ArchiveController ..> NfsConnectionDialog

}

' =====================================================================
' Filesystem SPI — no extension point, hardcoded drivers
' =====================================================================
package "Filesystem (OCP / DIP violated)" #FFEBEB {

  class FileSystemFactory <<BAD: OCP violation>> <<hardcoded>> {
    -drivers : Map<String, FileSystemDriver>
    --
    -registerDefaults() : void
    +open(URI, Map) : FileSystem
  }
  note top of FileSystemFactory
    registerDefaults() hard-codes
    "zip" / "weefs" / "nfs" drivers.
    Adding a scheme requires editing
    the factory → OCP violation.
  end note

  interface FileSystemDriver
  class ZipFileSystemDriver <<BAD: DIP violation>> {
    -provider : ExtZipFsProvider
    --
    +ZipFileSystemDriver()
  }
  class NfsFileSystemDriver <<BAD: DIP violation>> {
    -provider : NfsSftpFsProvider
    --
    +NfsFileSystemDriver()
  }
  note bottom of NfsFileSystemDriver
    Driver calls `new NfsSftpFsProvider()`
    internally → no injection, untestable,
    impossible to swap.
  end note

  FileSystemDriver <|.. ZipFileSystemDriver
  FileSystemDriver <|.. NfsFileSystemDriver
  FileSystemFactory o--> FileSystemDriver

  ' --- supporting base classes ---
  class ExtZipFileSystem <<base: weefs FS>>
  class ExtZipFsProvider <<base: weefs FS>>
  class NfsSftpFsProvider <<base: NFS FS>>
  ZipFileSystemDriver --> ExtZipFsProvider
  NfsFileSystemDriver --> NfsSftpFsProvider
  ExtZipFsProvider --> ExtZipFileSystem
}

' =====================================================================
' Archive extraction — monolithic, if/else over format
' =====================================================================
package "Extractor (no Strategy)" #FFEBEB {

  class Extractor <<BAD: monolithic>> <<big-switch>> {
    --
    +extractZip(Path, Path) : void
    +extractTar(Path, Path) : void
    +extractGz(Path, Path) : void
    +writeZip(Path, Path) : void
    +writeTar(Path, Path) : void
    +detectFormat(Path) : String
  }
  note bottom of Extractor
    One class does every archive format.
    Adding a format means editing Extractor
    and its callers → OCP + Strategy missing.
  end note
}

' =====================================================================
' Compression — no strategy abstraction, ad-hoc gzip path
' =====================================================================
package "Compression (no abstraction)" #FFEBEB {

  class AdHocGzipUsage <<BAD: no Strategy>> {
    --
    +wrapStream(InputStream, String) : InputStream
  }
  note bottom of AdHocGzipUsage
    Compression selected inline with
    if (isGzip) new GZIPInputStream(...)
    scattered across call sites.
  end note
}

' =====================================================================
' NFS — transport not pooled
' =====================================================================
package "NFS (no pooling)" #FFEBEB {

  class NfsSftpFsIO <<BAD: no pooling>> {
    -jsch : JSch
    --
    +withChannel(SftpWork) : T
  }
  note bottom of NfsSftpFsIO
    A fresh SSH session + SFTP channel
    is opened per operation. Expensive;
    no reuse, no timeout management.
  end note
}

' =====================================================================
' Cross-package wiring — shows concrete coupling
' =====================================================================
ArchiveModel --> FileSystemFactory
ArchiveModel --> NfsSftpFsIO
ArchiveController --> ArchiveModel
ArchiveController --> NfsFileOperations
ArchiveController --> FileOperations
ArchiveController ..> Extractor
MainFrame --> ArchiveController

' =====================================================================
' Legend
' =====================================================================
legend right
  == Anti-patterns captured in this view ==
  • God object — ArchiveModel owns every UI / mount / NFS concern
  • Single-session — only one archive can be open at a time
  • Duplicate state — controller mirrors model's NFS config
  • Concrete leak — controller returns NfsFileOperations, views hold ArchiveController
  • No IFileOperations seam — DIP violated at file-ops layer
  • Hardcoded factory — FileSystemFactory.registerDefaults() violates OCP
  • New'd providers — drivers construct providers internally (DIP)
  • Monolithic Extractor — one class, big switch over format
  • No compression Strategy — gzip/xz wrapping scattered inline
  • No SSH pooling — NfsSftpFsIO opens a session per operation
  • No clipboard — UI has no copy/cut/paste abstraction
  • Tight view→controller coupling — MainFrame binds to concrete ArchiveController
  Each <<BAD: ...>> stereotype maps to a fix in the good-design view.
endlegend
@enduml
